      "worked_solution": "The tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A). \n\nRelative to the angle $\\theta ,$ the length of the opposite side is $6x-5,$ and the length of the adjacent side is $4x.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}} \\\\ \\frac{15}{12} & =\\frac{6x-5}{4x} \\\\ 60x & =72x-60 \\\\ 12x & =60 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
